[N 1-6 Zephras Isle]
[D Forever Warrior 1-30 (Braedyn)\\Built 1 Nov 2026 from QuestieDB Forever 1.0.9 and the Wowhead Zephras Isle pull of 1 Nov 2026; step order checked against Polestar 0.2.6 and TUGs.\\Skyborne Protection Warrior: Thendal Grove, level 1 to the road south to Shen'dar.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffZephras Isle 1-6|r  -  the Skyborne start in Thendal Grove (Skyborne Protection Warrior, 1H + shield). Horde and other-class quests on the island are not in this guide.
[OC][A Warrior] |cffffcc00Gear rule:|r one-hand weapon + shield from the first shield reward on; mail at any level, then leather (no plate until 40). Stats: weapon dps > Str > Sta > Agi > Armor; Defense is low value while levelling, real in dungeons. Weights: docs/forever-prot-stat-weights.md (reasoning only, nothing tested in game).
[OC]|cffffcc00Professions (Forever):|r |cff66ff66Skinning + Mining first|r, plus First Aid + Cooking + Fishing. Why not Blacksmithing: Forever's tank mail set (Guard's: Str/Sta/Defense) needs about 34 Shadowgem and 22 Pristine Leather by level 25 - both Scarce drops - so it cannot be crafted without rare-drop farms. Passives: Skinning = +5% damage to Beasts and Dragonkin, Mining = +5% total health. There are no profession trainers in Thendal Grove: you learn them on arrival in Shen'dar (6-14 Zephras Isle), except that the Harvesting Windstones reward book below teaches Skinning here.
[OC]|cffffcc00Cooking + Fishing plan (Forever):|r your food ladder is Roasted Boar Meat (+1 Str, trainer) -> |cff66ff66Longjaw Mud Snapper (+10 attack power, level 5+)|r -> |cff66ff66Mithril Head Trout (+20 attack power, level 25+)|r. Both fish come from your own fishing rod, so Fishing is part of this guide: learn it in Shen'dar (6-14 Zephras Isle), buy Khara Deepwater's Strong Fishing Pole (+45 Fishing in Forever) at the loch, and fish where the guide says "fish to N". Skill targets: Cooking 50 by 12 (Journeyman at Daryl Riknussun, Ironforge), 80 by 16, 125 by 24 (Expert Cookbook from Shandrina, Ashenvale), 175 by ~30 for the trout; Fishing 25 by 12, 50 by 15 (Journeyman at Grimnur Stonebrand, Ironforge), 100 by 22, 130+ by 28. Every other recipe on the route is a skill-up filler: cook whatever meat you loot and eat the best thing you have.
[OC]|cffffcc00Camping (Forever):|r Cooking 1 teaches the Basic Campfire (3 object slots). Sit or craft at a fire for 1 minute to get its buffs (1 hour). Each player adds ONE profession object: your Lodestone (Mining 20) = melee attack power, your Camp Chair (Skinning 20) = +2% crit, First Aid Kit = stamina, Fish Bowl (Fishing 20; does not stack with Blessing of Kings) = +8% all stats, Leatherworking tent = rested XP. Objects have a 1-hour cooldown and the fire vanishes after ~10-15 min, so set camp right before a dungeon or a long grind, with your friend adding his object. The Camping 101 quests (level 6, Raan Wildwind outside Shen'dar) teach the tier-1 objects once that skill is 20.
[OC]|cffffcc00Skyborne (unverified):|r racials Walk on Air (slow fall / glide - two quests here use it), +2% haste, +5% damage vs Elementals, Read Ley Line (regeneration at ley lines; one quest here uses it). Zephras Isle has no inn, hearth or flight master; the tornadoes on the island give +40% run speed for 5 minutes - run through them.
[OC]|cffffcc00Launch rule (1-6):|r no shared tags in Forever - on a camped named mob (the Cirrusfly Queen, Urs'anah the Den Mother, Malduko Cloudcrush) INVITE the people standing there (kill credit shares in a party; most drop items don't). If no group forms in ~2 min, tick the step and keep moving; the catch-up line before you leave the grove brings you back. Expect the first 10-20 min to be the worst.

